Third-party software
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OpenMDVR depends on the following open-source projects. They are NOT
redistributed in this repository (they are fetched by the Go, Python and npm
package managers, or downloaded while building container images), and each
remains under its own license:

Media / video
  - ZLMediaKit (MIT) - https://github.com/ZLMediaKit/ZLMediaKit
    infra/zlmediakit/audio-transcode.patch is derived from ZLMediaKit's
    upstream branch feature/transcode2 and remains under the MIT license,
    Copyright (c) 2016-present The ZLMediaKit project authors.
  - FFmpeg (LGPL-2.1+ / GPL-2.0+) - https://ffmpeg.org
    The custom ZLMediaKit image built by infra/zlmediakit/Dockerfile links the
    FFmpeg libraries packaged by Ubuntu, which are built with GPL components.
    If you distribute that built image, you must comply with FFmpeg's license
    terms (including providing the corresponding source). This repository
    only contains the Dockerfile, not FFmpeg itself.
  - mpegts.js (Apache-2.0) - https://github.com/xqq/mpegts.js
  - Plyr (MIT) - https://github.com/sampotts/plyr

Protocol / server (Go)
  - go-jt808 (MIT) - https://github.com/cuteLittleDevil/go-jt808
  - pgx (MIT) - https://github.com/jackc/pgx
  - AWS SDK for Go v2 (Apache-2.0) - https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2
  - google/uuid (BSD-3-Clause), golang.org/x/sync (BSD-3-Clause)

API (Python)
  - FastAPI (MIT), Uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause), Pydantic (MIT), HTTPX (BSD-3-Clause),
    PyJWT (MIT), bcrypt (Apache-2.0), boto3 (Apache-2.0),
    email-validator (Unlicense/CC0)
  - psycopg 3 (LGPL-3.0) - used unmodified as a library

Database
  - PostgreSQL (PostgreSQL License)
  - TimescaleDB (Apache-2.0 for the community edition features used here)

Web dashboard
  - React, React DOM (MIT), React Router (MIT), Vite (MIT), Tailwind CSS (MIT)
  - Leaflet (BSD-2-Clause), leaflet.markercluster (MIT),
    react-leaflet-cluster (MIT), Leaflet.hotline (BSD-2-Clause)
  - react-leaflet and @react-leaflet/core (Hippocratic License 2.1). This is
    not an OSI-approved license and adds use restrictions; it applies to the
    built web bundle. Replacing react-leaflet with plain Leaflet is tracked
    on the roadmap.
  - MapLibre GL JS (BSD-3-Clause), @maplibre/maplibre-gl-leaflet (ISC)
  - lucide-react (ISC)

Run `npx license-checker --production` in web/ and `go-licenses report ./...`
in jt808-server/ for the authoritative, version-exact list.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Map data
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Map tiles are loaded at runtime from third-party providers and are subject to
their terms and attribution requirements, which the UI displays:
  - OpenStreetMap data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0
  - OpenFreeMap / OpenMapTiles
  - Esri World Imagery / World Street Map (Esri terms of use)
  - CARTO basemaps (optional, requires your own API key)

